# Icon reference sets — third-party SVG sources used for redesign work.
# The top-level _svg/*.svg files (ngwr originals) stay tracked; only the
# per-source subdirectories are ignored.
projects/lib/icon/_svg/lucide/
projects/lib/icon/_svg/phosphor/
projects/lib/icon/_svg/tabler/
projects/lib/icon/_svg/heroicons/

# Generated by release/publish workflows (pnpm release:body) — never tracked.
.release-body.md

# AI assistant artifacts — the shared instructions ARE tracked (AGENTS.md plus
# the root CLAUDE.md / GEMINI.md pointers). These are per-developer state,
# history, and local config that must never be committed.
.claude/
.gemini/
.aider*

# Generated AI assets. Both come from scripts/gen-ai-assets.ts, and only ONE of
# them is ignored — sitemap.xml is emitted straight into the (ignored) dist by
# scripts/gen-sitemap.ts.
#
# `skills/` used to be listed here too, and it contradicted the repository: the
# three files under `skills/ngwr/` are TRACKED on purpose, because the skill
# ships inside the npm tarball and a stale committed copy is a real failure —
# it once sat two entry points behind for a whole release. Since .gitignore
# does not apply to files already tracked, the rule changed nothing for those
# three and only armed a trap for the fourth: `gen-ai-assets.ts` deletes and
# recreates that directory on every build, so a NEW reference file would have
# been ignored, never committed, and shipped from disk by copy-dist-assets
# while the repository knew nothing about it.
llms-full.txt

# Root-level markdown, allowlisted. Every document that belongs at the root is
# named below; anything else there is a scratch file.
#
# This exists because one was not caught: `ngwr-pagination-issue.md`, a 188-line
# issue draft, rode into the v14 release commit and stayed for 46 commits — long
# enough to ship inside the source tree of v14.0.0, v14.0.1, v14.1.0 and v14.2.0,
# where anyone browsing the tag found it next to README.md. Nothing in `pnpm
# lint` reads the repository root, so no gate could have said anything.
#
# Adding a root document now costs one deliberate line here, which is the point.
/*.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/GEMINI.md
!/MIGRATION.md
!/README.md
!/ROADMAP.md
!/SECURITY.md
